{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "metadata": {
    "id": "murmur-dune-worm-call",
    "name": "WORM CALL",
    "author": "Patchwork Eight Engineering",
    "description": "Dune-film-score-aesthetic patch: an inharmonic, bandpass-formed growl -- a 'call' rather than a pad. INHARMONIC via an 8-operator stack at deliberately non-integer frequency ratios (1.02, 3.02, 4.976, 6.03, 7.97) layered over a root and two sub operators, producing bell/metallic beating without a dedicated Resonator engine (not yet implemented -- see AlgorithmTypes.hpp isEngineImplemented). FORMANT/VOCAL via Filter 1 in bandpass mode at 650Hz with high resonance and strong keytrack, so the 'call' character follows pitch. ALIEN/EVOLVING via a Freq-Shift Echo insert (+37Hz, feedback 0.55) whose repeats drift progressively out of tune with each pass -- a genuinely alien, non-integer-ratio shimmer that builds over the note's sustain -- plus LFO1 -> FilterCutoff for a wobbling formant and Velocity -> FilterCutoff so a hard hit snarls brighter. A rendered preview of this patch (parameter-surface-only, since mod routes below aren't reachable via a plain VST3 parameter list) is at scratchpad/dune/worm_call.wav / the published 'Dune Session' artifact -- the mod routes here make the real loaded patch noticeably more alive than that preview.",
    "category": "texture",
    "moods": [
      "dark",
      "alien",
      "growling",
      "evolving",
      "cinematic"
    ],
    "genres": [
      "score",
      "sound-design"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "dune",
      "inharmonic",
      "freq-shift",
      "bandpass"
    ],
